[{:db/id "q-80347/selection/7ea009d38067b85c260cd71ce15cce585e1f931f7adf440bc470127b22bd36c2" :answer/id #uuid "3e809a76-295b-5781-86b5-2dbb9b038ca8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral is divergent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80347/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "cf61fc6a-da22-5e24-ac86-dd81e6de1add" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80347/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "b5967994-25c4-5a1c-9821-3b5c46d6cdb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80347/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "beed96ca-eee6-57f1-9425-964fba906eb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80347/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4e5f5d69-1902-50fd-b3fc-84fbfabe1369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80347/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9100afc8-dba2-5771-9b67-77e4a9c47211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80347/selection/7ea009d38067b85c260cd71ce15cce585e1f931f7adf440bc470127b22bd36c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-80347/selection/7ea009d38067b85c260cd71ce15cce585e1f931f7adf440bc470127b22bd36c2" "q-80347/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-80347/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-80347/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-80347/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80347" :question/id #uuid "9b00f298-c8ee-513b-9db1-ba9601a75ae2" :question/math-academy-id "q-80347" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u=8-{x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=8-{x}^{3}$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & -1 & -\\infty  \\\\ u & 9 & \\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\infty }^{9}(-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{9}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{9}^{a}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[2\\sqrt{u}]}_{9}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{9}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\infty  \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80347/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc6d9b69-0459-515a-ba7b-c62cab96ca00"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-100642/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "80258669-7f1e-5c89-b51f-db152c3d9e02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100642/selection/7ea009d38067b85c260cd71ce15cce585e1f931f7adf440bc470127b22bd36c2" :answer/id #uuid "131ed8cf-747f-57c3-92db-fa739e9f69dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral is divergent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100642/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "f112d95a-72a1-56c6-948d-0e6679b3bbf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100642/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "151c80c4-9585-5392-a64c-59c3b41f64e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100642/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "672e99c0-2eca-58c8-923d-56020cbabdd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100642/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "565a878f-a0fc-521d-b11f-9bb2d78ce72e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-100642/selection/7ea009d38067b85c260cd71ce15cce585e1f931f7adf440bc470127b22bd36c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-100642/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-100642/selection/7ea009d38067b85c260cd71ce15cce585e1f931f7adf440bc470127b22bd36c2" "q-100642/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-100642/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-100642/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-100642" :question/id #uuid "e05c5658-b5b1-574e-bc85-31bf0c6c3511" :question/math-academy-id "q-100642" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{2z+1}}\\,\\text{d}z=$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{2z+1}}\\,\\text{d}z & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{2z+1}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{3}{2}(2z+1)^{2/3}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[(2z+1)^{2/3}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }((2a+1)^{2/3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\infty  \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-100642/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc6d9b69-0459-515a-ba7b-c62cab96ca00"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-100642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152056/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" :answer/id #uuid "376ba64f-a707-53fb-b80d-c882ba4dd961" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152056/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" :answer/id #uuid "28e28573-5dd7-5891-995b-6c3e5dfd78d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152056/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "d4f29ab4-ba48-5124-a3ea-8a49861f5fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152056/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" :answer/id #uuid "f94f4f8c-588e-5663-bbbc-0a832258d008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152056/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "5053871c-5dfd-5bc4-afe4-d6389e446520" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152056/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c41a572-1358-5776-afe2-d497131fa388" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152056/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" :answer-field/choices ["q-152056/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" "q-152056/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" "q-152056/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-152056/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" "q-152056/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152056" :question/id #uuid "5f87941f-f51b-5324-9c4e-72f9bdb927d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-152056" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}+1)^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u={x}^{3}+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{3}+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}+1)^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{u}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{u}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{-3/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{a}^{3}}}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-152056/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6dc2621a-77e1-56d9-af63-1917eaa933b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152056"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350527/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "470f44d2-9390-5f11-b444-dd05fbe28bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350527/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "d82a8af2-a9d2-5893-9473-6c317042b707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350527/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2687e102-dbc8-5a47-83cf-a7c46cd972ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350527/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-350527/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-350527/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350527" :question/id #uuid "dc89d030-e379-5939-8c83-6d032affef6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-350527" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u=x+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=x+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }3{u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}3{u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{3}{4}{u}^{-4}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-4}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{4}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-350527/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6dc2621a-77e1-56d9-af63-1917eaa933b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350543/field-1/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" :answer/id #uuid "95a5be23-15ec-5717-b0bb-c93855685dfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350543/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ed6de76-499a-535b-8349-07e4cb8e1e06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350543/field-1/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-350543/field-1/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350543" :question/id #uuid "41c4f6a7-69db-5812-9f0a-6a2ff4b7b713" :question/math-academy-id "q-350543" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{12}{(5\\theta -1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $u=5\\theta -1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=5\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $\\theta \\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=5\\theta -1$ is as follows:\n\n| $\\theta $ | $-\\infty $ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{12}{(5\\theta -1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{12}{5{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{12}{5{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{12}{5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{u}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-{u}^{-1}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{u}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-1)}-\\frac{1}{a}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot (-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-350543/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39a476b5-eacc-59c1-9d16-fc0675e3bc12"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350543"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
